    ],
    "rules": [
      "parser.y:workbookref STRING explicitly queries sheetless name scope and reports UNKNOWN_NAME when absent; it never adds a placeholder.",
      "parser_simple_name creates placeholders only for unqualified or sheet-qualified names when lookup fails.",
      "xml_sax_cell reports failed ordinary-cell parsing, then stores the original expression text as a constant string."
    ]
  },
  "problem": "The XML name binder created #NAME? global placeholders for []Name even when no declaration/placeholder existed at that parse point; native workbookref STRING rejects these names and the XML cell parser stores the rejected expression as a constant string.",
  "implementation": [
    "Track the first qualified-name rejection in existing XML binding traversal, including missing local sheets, and stop later name-creation side effects.",
    "Preserve earlier unqualified placeholders; explicitly global names can use them or earlier declarations, but cannot bind to a declaration appearing later.",
    "Ordinary cells recover original expression text with a gnumeric-xml warning. Shared followers reuse the recovered constant; positive array corners retain their separate path.",
    "Remove the duplicate later missing-sheet parse pass, preserving native source-order selection between explicit-global and missing-sheet name errors."
  ],
